#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142636 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5587f6-f6a7-523c-b532-15786ade73b7" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Whole Number by a Non-Unit Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "23532ee6-f05b-5ac7-b722-84891afd3bc5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14197" :question/problem "![](images/45/45d4e4ca4f1cdfddcb624dccf32cb053818a2fd70cbb7b5a02d1ff30f9784e2b.png)\n\n \n\nThe model above represents $3$ wholes. Use the model to determine the missing number in the following division problem. \n![](images/a0/a0f8afd7559875c611abbeede5718b107447300e263bc8c71e69c046a89de15c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split each whole into fifths.\n\n![](images/9c/9c10c283125b23a553855e247149fba126c1977bf62a487b09121eb539dabfbf.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups of ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac3{5}}}.$\n\n![](images/a8/a8ee616adc072552e64182bba65bd74754b4a16857bfc7fe7e411ab9784bd331.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, we count the groups.\n\n![](images/ad/ad9c3bcb60e6277ae536b00489b3f4267a31fb9f2d0a7af368ee0cc43215287d.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $\\color{blue}3$ wholes into groups of ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac3{5}}},$ we get ${\\color{purple}{5}}$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n3 \\div \\dfrac{3}{{5}} = \\fbox{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the missing number is $\\bbox[3pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{purple}5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142637 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142846 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c692a59-11d5-5b7c-868c-438cfd23a04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Two Missing Numbers"}] :question/id #uuid "be59814b-3823-57b9-9a2c-f678e1d34183" :question/math-academy-id "e-14203" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0c3f53204a0271ea9816eaddbdbeeb84648638918531ace2f06251af765fe05f.png)\n\n \n\nUse the model above to determine the missing numbers in the following division problem.\n![](images/ac/acfcba0a6dd2c27a2d02996f6c1574dca601e0f1afaa4fe45a9cc3ed8c5a1012.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by interpreting our model:\n\n- The model shows $\\color{blue}2$ wholes. Each whole is split into *thirds*.\n\n![](images/d9/d9c692ed44d98c47b475dc18c2d28a01d0ab1f2f231ed24a9604f14000f599b1.png)\n\n \n\n- The thirds are grouped, and each group contains ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac23}}.$\n\n![](images/3c/3c9fd6222f68deffa02ce69a2f31dca220ce2285f71dbd8255d364126ea0d8c8.png)\n\n \n\n- There are $\\color{purple} 3$ groups in total.\n\n![](images/22/228c9e5eea2b5696d64d4423ecd927e12a11e6672d614cc30a947549943be0c4.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $\\color{blue}2$ wholes into groups of ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac23}},$ we get ${\\color{purple}{3}}$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, the model represents the following division problem:\n![](images/36/36c793809763d52bf4acade045eab9b76235e47ae4c72dcc3a699c2891231f76.svg)\n\nTherefore, the missing numbers are $\\bbox[3pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}2}$ and $\\bbox[3pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{purple}3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142655 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f7df9be-867f-56b1-85d3-00ad838dc054" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Number"}] :question/id #uuid "7f3801c4-d25f-57e0-85b3-b52df08d7072" :question/math-academy-id "e-15654" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7fbc79b1d259f645a8296be12c2748e5abb05d02217f3628e24ef20781f06c71.png)\n\n \n\nUse the model above to determine the missing number in the following division problem. \n![](images/f6/f603ac2cbe9286f62209217ba0b8a5a3cf239b463266f78493a2d6f321737c07.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by interpreting our model:\n\n- The model shows $\\color{blue}4$ wholes. Each whole is split into *fifths*.\n\n![](images/20/2096f3451d19fc44bccca9ebe3033e9af29878aa928ad05b102e391be3f76105.png)\n\n \n\n- The fifths are grouped, and each group contains ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac{2}{5}}}.$\n\n![](images/96/96bc693ffe7fa65c90758e0d86a7176b19f7a279cfff12607926e0350448fe42.png)\n\n \n\n- There are $\\color{purple} 10$ groups in total.\n\n![](images/1e/1ebdc6bce6be33bbdd5fd7ff79a562c22e68103cebc8f0ded5ddac6833633989.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $\\color{blue}4$ wholes into groups of ${\\color{red}{\\dfrac{2}{5}}},$ we get ${\\color{purple}{10}}$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, the model represents the following division problem:\n![](images/3b/3b00de3e8e69546d481290c7f9b490cc290ae40b71ba19faf0da93f49be5532c.svg)\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\bbox[3pt, Gainsboro]{\\color{red}\\dfrac{2}{5}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440730 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142847 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe5587f6-f6a7-523c-b532-15786ade73b7" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Whole Number by a Non-Unit Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8604638b-33e5-5189-9a29-241003eeb47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8604638b-33e5-5189-9a29-241003eeb47c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440684} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6dcd2f7-e45a-5a85-84ee-9eac085ab6f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbdd1be3-40cc-5245-8bb6-12f602066273" :question/math-academy-id "q-174115" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4ddb2ab8a612594044f57cbba499b8d398979ea4376d5a3fcaaec0ca5bdfe7e9.png)\n\nIf the model above represents $2$ wholes, use the model to solve the following division problem. Express your answer as a whole number.\n\n$2÷\\frac{2}{6}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We proceed as follows:\n\n- First, we split each whole into sixths.\n\n![](images/0f/0f1ad639c2ea37dd2cd777ef01f7fe51acd1a90c1afa6782698a188f61c63381.png)\n\n \n\n- Next, we create groups of $\\frac{2}{6}.$\n\n![](images/17/17806a28d4b4dd3f604030460809a43a1282c3f06b412fa4a3a2f4fcb43e47d2.png)\n\n \n\n- Then, we count the groups.\n\n![](images/cc/cc0f841b8652f3589b381c9f434afccaab62bf8ea691ee6fdd0edd4776f24694.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $2$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{2}{6},$ we get $6$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2÷\\frac{2}{6}=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f7df9be-867f-56b1-85d3-00ad838dc054" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20f19fa8-8441-5f89-b438-5d393df3bd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440663} {:answer/id #uuid "230d5819-565f-5aa5-bf0b-319c1f9cc9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440665} {:answer/id #uuid "78c4f1d3-20fa-57ed-9622-6ba114e21834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440680} {:answer/id #uuid "9a724afb-c111-564b-b096-958ef8cb5993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440692} {:answer/id #uuid "a892f328-21aa-5c76-85c2-395dd96254c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c4f1d3-20fa-57ed-9622-6ba114e21834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440680} :answer-field/id #uuid "def84f61-dd13-597e-adff-b89bcc510da0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440716}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b0b3ca4-9ff0-5255-978a-4bfe3963f6ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-237473" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca9db09a0ca6ad110fb2c2f00be45d457d2d4e654034115d42a0a1b93e1c7417.png)\n\nUse the model above to determine the missing number in the following division problem. \n\n$$\n3÷\\boxed{\\,\\,}=5\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by interpreting our model:\n\n- The model shows $3$ wholes. Each whole is split into *fifths*.\n\n![](images/44/44fb9e1227b086564f4992529d6fd9308e1eb0d8b197b55e7e56afa98b8d76a4.png)\n\n \n\n- The fifths are grouped, and each group contains $\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\n![](images/0a/0abe764e73534f4ea5fe9bbe5a942fd7257a4ceca6992796c450e5760051f124.png)\n\n \n\n- There are $5$ groups in total.\n\n![](images/e8/e858a032d27681d19dc411f4aa59215f8e1ac9546cdd964a017893d3004d445f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $3$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{3}{5},$ we get $5$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, the model represents the following division problem:\n\n$$\n3÷\\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}=5\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\frac{3}{5}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440727 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f7df9be-867f-56b1-85d3-00ad838dc054" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18abbae6-c813-5bf9-a1b7-288e0b1309ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440661} {:answer/id #uuid "82f619b1-4278-5ce4-a18a-61d597cc8d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440682} {:answer/id #uuid "86facde6-f01b-5692-8f94-833fb81cf2aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440685} {:answer/id #uuid "eb64d029-b998-5f89-9ac0-fb7e713eb617" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440701} {:answer/id #uuid "ffca9a28-f997-5afb-afb4-2a49f0152852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440703}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffca9a28-f997-5afb-afb4-2a49f0152852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440703} :answer-field/id #uuid "661c11cd-7ff8-502f-8aa8-a24571ecfa89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "776a8568-74b6-50c2-b082-415a4e4bc0bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-237483" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa0a9630bbc293b8e8eb5c60f7050b2481d33a06b57ed6b19527e14b834fe5f1.png)\n\nUse the model above to determine the missing number in the following division problem. \n\n$$\n2÷\\boxed{\\,\\,}=3\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by interpreting our model:\n\n- The model shows $2$ wholes. Each whole is split into *sixths*.\n\n![](images/ec/ec09e83087ba7ada6af5cf1d2d19e4260a4581f2818659ebedc902f8edf13250.png)\n\n \n\n- The sixths are grouped, and each group contains $\\frac{4}{6}.$\n\n![](images/83/83ab830b24af9dddc5bb84d4496e440e4bb9d033b07df506001073a4b994a181.png)\n\n \n\n- There are $3$ groups in total.\n\n![](images/e7/e7f2afcd0b6d934b639d96300d9fc149d15beebdef4dc4b3541677f6eb9d6de2.png)\n\n \n\nSo, if we divide $2$ wholes into groups of $\\frac{4}{6},$ we get $3$ groups in total.\n\nTherefore, the model represents the following division problem:\n\n$$\n2÷\\boxed{\\frac{4}{6}}=3\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\frac{4}{6}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f7df9be-867f-56b1-85d3-00ad838dc054" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Missing Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abd57b7-57f5-52a1-8dac-9e1e4bc07512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440658} {:answer/id #uuid "2c760dcc-fd4a-506e-8cf2-064f23afc792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440667} {:answer/id #uuid "5240675c-2169-586e-9491-07c2c018a767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440673} {:answer/id #uuid "83f6eefc-efd0-5db1-833c-9b2f811838e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440683} {:answer/id #uuid "daec4bd0-21e2-596a-bbbe-a35b41d3d86c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0abd57b7-57f5-52a1-8dac-9e1e4bc07512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440658} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce77ac91-10b8-5fa5-8266-ee037bb8f3d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70508159-98d6-5f24-aff9-401cfa300d66" :question/math-academy-id "q-237486" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4fb4cd078511a6fc3c7bc